NativeAOT's link for witos through the SDK's targets (plan step R2.3b, RFC 0015 section 9): the system layer's
toolchain is clang with lld for the triple <arch>-unknown-linux-musl, as for FreeBSD's branch; WitOS builds no GSSAPI
shim, so System.Net.Security.Native is not linked, while System.Security.Cryptography.Native.OpenSsl is, as on Linux,
since W3.1 (the OpenSSL the system layer builds; the portable shim opens its libraries at run time); the
runtime is built against libc++ (CLR_CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD_LIBRARY, R1.2b), so the program links libc++, whose ABI
library has the __cxa_thread_atexit the runtime's thread_local destructors call. V2.4: no -latomic on witos, whose sysroot has no libatomic; the 16-byte compare-exchange riscv64's PalInterlockedCompareExchange128 needs comes from compiler-rt's atomic.c in the sysroot's builtins.

